# Whole V3 plus single-owner publication: scoped source review — 22 October 2026

**Result: no actionable source finding in the reviewed combination.** This is a read-only review of the 10-file diff against `83ccb82314f84449aa14c269f09b0da43cf65e2e`, not a gate result or an admission decision. Product remains frozen at `dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7`; the original four-file V3 patch is authenticated by SHA-256 `02e2d697cf08f95abee99170abc47b71012f5653ba31ab21e7a7bcfffa7ca2b6`. No tests, builds, formatters, benchmarks, browser checks, or Git mutations were run in this review.

The full-range path is reachable only after `prepare_retained_order(Gather)` creates the pending-plus-unpublished renderer-order scratch. `planner_full_frontier_source_range` then requires every active owner exactly once in order, existing ranges contiguous in **both** source and record coordinates, unchanged source counts, no active or committed decorations, and full unpublished intervals where an interval list exists. It also requires a positive final source end equal to `gathered_source_count`. Missing owners, partial/scattered intervals, stale/noncontiguous ranges, changed topology, decorations, and empty or invalid frontiers decline admission and use the existing `OwnerRanges` iterator or the existing replacement/fresh route. `None` intervals are intentionally a full-recomposition case; the shared callback still consults per-row semantic masks and validates owner transitions. `PlannerState::paragraph` uses binary search, so the new admission has O(N log P) owner lookup cost and does not prove a net lookup deletion.

On admission, `RetainedRanges` emits one `0..end` range into the existing single ordered rope traversal. The callback still advances the ordered owner iterator, visits source rows, resolves bindings, and runs Codec work. A count mismatch or callback Stop retains suffix rebuild; callback/storage errors restore `self.sources` after the transactional rope operation. The cloned prior source root remains scoped to that call. The frozen single-owner preflight and `publication_ack_only_visits` remain present. `commit_paragraphs(true)` handles pending IDs before unpublished IDs and skips the older unpublished acknowledgement for an owner with a newer pending preparation. Full-frontier admission runs before publication acknowledgement clears intervals and masks.

The dense 1,024-owner state fixture now reads a pending replacement through measurement/layout inspection, copies its current glyphs into an independently encoded plan, overwrites that owner twice, and verifies detached payload/session bytes before and after publication. It keeps the accepted physical draw/binding order, active Codec buffers, and placement-byte comparison against a separately built cold scene. The Codec fixture also compares a 1,024-owner full-range gather with fresh gather, while the Stop and callback-failure tests exercise both iterator modes; scattered input asserts owner-range fallback. Existing integration tests exercise prepared measure/glyph/caret/split and a first split surviving later edits. These are sound proof designs, but their assertions have not yet been executed on this combined checkout.

Failed renderer delivery plus the new 1,024-owner pending overwrite and detached-copy sequence is not exercised as one test. Source inspection shows delivery failure invalidates the derived root through `invalidate_after_publication_failure`, and existing reset/replay and seeded abort/retry tests cover that transition separately. This is a precise coverage limit, not a demonstrated bug in the combined path. The native full-range counters are test-only; they cannot establish the timed Wasm path or its row counts. The benchmark changes add `@frontier` only under the four intended names' conditions, register the suite, and leave callback bodies unchanged. Suite resolution must still show exactly those four identities before timing.

Luna's remaining gates are the named native and package integration tests, workflow routing, authenticated native/Wasm artifacts, renderer publication, and the bounded fixed-20 single-call eight-block comparison of the four callbacks. Keep every sample and block distribution. Select this variant only if both dense complete operations improve reproducibly, both guards avoid credible regression, and the required full seven-family comparison against current main and published 0.1.0 plus size/memory/output gates pass. The frozen dense candidate medians of 8.294/17.485 ms versus main 6.933/15.193 ms establish existing ordinary loss, not a V3 result; the historical 113 ms stall is unresolved and is not a tail veto or a reason to rerun selectively.
